{"id": 8, "ts": 1779487038.278789, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I\u2019d like to add a couple of observations from my interview that may affect our assessment of reliability and crew cooperation. Candidate\u202fB, while very conscientious and stress\u2011resilient, demonstrated a relatively weak memory for numbers during the technical exercise, and several references noted that he can make nasty remarks toward colleagues. Both issues raise concerns about operational reliability (especially for long\u2011haul flight planning) and professional communication.\nCandidate\u202fD, on the other hand, impressed with concentration, problem\u2011solving and a strong sense of responsibility, but I observed a hot\u2011temper episode in a simulated emergency debrief and received feedback that he can come across as a know\u2011it\u2011all, which could hinder crew harmony on extended missions.\nGiven these points, I\u2019m leaning toward **Candidate\u202fD** as the provisional choice, provided we can verify that his temperament can be managed and that he can cooperate effectively with the crew. I suggest we gather any additional evidence on crew\u2011cooperation behaviors for both B and D before finalizing.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_2\", \"vote\": \"Candidate D\"}"}
